{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Convolutions from Scratch Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Pad an array"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Start with the smallest primitive: a function that pads with zeros around an H x W array."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def pad2d(x, p):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if p == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    h, w = x.shape[-2:]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = np.zeros(x.shape[:-2] + (h + 2 * p, w + 2 * p), dtype=x.dtype)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out[..., p:p + h, p:p + w] = x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = np.arange(9).reshape(3, 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(pad2d(x, 1))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The trailing-axes trick `x.shape[:-2]` means the same function works on `(H, W)`, `(C, H, W)`, or `(N, C, H, W)` without modification."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: 2D convolution with nested loops"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The reference implementation \u2014 slow, but unambiguous. This is what `torch.nn.functional.conv2d` does in principle."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def conv2d_naive(x, w, b=None, stride=1, padding=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    c_in, h, w_in = x.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    c_out, c_in_w, kh, kw = w.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    assert c_in == c_in_w"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x_pad = pad2d(x, padding)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    h_out = (h + 2 * padding - kh) // stride + 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    w_out = (w_in + 2 * padding - kw) // stride + 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = np.zeros((c_out, h_out, w_out), dtype=np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for oc in range(c_out):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(h_out):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for j in range(w_out):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                hs = i * stride"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                ws = j * stride"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                patch = x_pad[:, hs:hs + kh, ws:ws + kw]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                out[oc, i, j] = np.sum(patch * w[oc])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if b is not None:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            out[oc] += b[oc]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Four nested loops (output channel, row, column, plus the implicit sum over C_in, kh, kw). This is the ground truth you will check every faster implementation against."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Verify with a hand-designed kernel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Build a vertical Sobel kernel, apply it to a synthetic step image, and watch the vertical edge light up."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def synthetic_step_image():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    img = np.zeros((1, 16, 16), dtype=np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    img[:, :, 8:] = 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return img"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "sobel_x = np.array(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    [[-1, 0, 1],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "     [-2, 0, 2],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "     [-1, 0, 1]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "], dtype=np.float32)[None]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = synthetic_step_image()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "y = conv2d_naive(x, sobel_x, padding=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(y[0].round(1))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Expect large positive values on column 7 (left-to-right brightness increase) and zeros everywhere else. That single print is your sanity check that the math is right."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: im2col"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Convert every kernel-sized window in the input into a column of a matrix. For `C_in=3, K=3`, each column is 27 numbers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def im2col(x, kh, kw, stride=1, padding=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    c_in, h, w = x.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x_pad = pad2d(x, padding)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    h_out = (h + 2 * padding - kh) // stride + 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    w_out = (w + 2 * padding - kw) // stride + 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cols = np.zeros((c_in * kh * kw, h_out * w_out), dtype=x.dtype)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    col = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(h_out):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for j in range(w_out):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            hs = i * stride"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ws = j * stride"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            patch = x_pad[:, hs:hs + kh, ws:ws + kw]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            cols[:, col] = patch.reshape(-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            col += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return cols, h_out, w_out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "It is still a Python loop, but now the heavy lifting will be a single vectorised matmul."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Fast conv via im2col + matmul"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Replace the quadruple loop with one matrix multiplication."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def conv2d_im2col(x, w, b=None, stride=1, padding=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    c_out, c_in, kh, kw = w.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cols, h_out, w_out = im2col(x, kh, kw, stride, padding)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    w_flat = w.reshape(c_out, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = w_flat @ cols"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if b is not None:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out += b[:, None]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return out.reshape(c_out, h_out, w_out)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Correctness check: run both implementations and compare."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "rng = np.random.default_rng(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = rng.normal(0, 1, (3, 16, 16)).astype(np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "w = rng.normal(0, 1, (8, 3, 3, 3)).astype(np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "b = rng.normal(0, 1, (8,)).astype(np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "y_naive = conv2d_naive(x, w, b, padding=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "y_im2col = conv2d_im2col(x, w, b, padding=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"max abs diff: {np.max(np.abs(y_naive - y_im2col)):.2e}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`max abs diff` should be around `1e-5` \u2014 the difference is floating-point accumulation order, not a bug."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: A bank of hand-designed kernels"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Five filters that show what a single conv layer can express before any training."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "KERNELS = {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"identity\": np.array([[0, 0, 0], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 0]], dtype=np.float32),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"blur_3x3\": np.ones((3, 3), dtype=np.float32) / 9.0,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"sharpen\": np.array([[0, -1, 0], [-1, 5, -1], [0, -1, 0]], dtype=np.float32),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"sobel_x\": np.array([[-1, 0, 1], [-2, 0, 2], [-1, 0, 1]], dtype=np.float32),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"sobel_y\": np.array([[-1, -2, -1], [0, 0, 0], [1, 2, 1]], dtype=np.float32),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def apply_kernel(img2d, kernel):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = img2d[None].astype(np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    w = kernel[None, None]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return conv2d_im2col(x, w, padding=1)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Applied to any grayscale image, blur softens, sharpen crisps up edges, Sobel-x lights up vertical edges, Sobel-y lights up horizontal edges. These are exactly the patterns that the *first* trained conv layer in AlexNet and VGG ended up learning \u2014 because a good image model needs edge and blob detectors no matter what task comes later."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Given a 128x128 grayscale input and a stack of `[Conv3x3(s=1,p=1), Conv3x3(s=2,p=1), Conv3x3(s=1,p=1), Conv3x3(s=2,p=1)]`, compute the output spatial size and the receptive field at each layer by hand. Verify with a PyTorch `nn.Sequential` of dummy convs.\n2. **(Medium)** Extend `conv2d_naive` and `conv2d_im2col` to accept a `groups` argument. Show that `groups=C_in=C_out` reproduces a depthwise convolution and that its parameter count is `C * K * K` instead of `C * C * K * K`.\n3. **(Hard)** Implement the backward pass of `conv2d_im2col` by hand: given the gradient of the output, compute the gradient of `x` and `w`. Verify against `torch.autograd.grad` on the same inputs and weights. The trick: the gradient of im2col is `col2im`, and it has to accumulate overlapping windows."
      ]
    }
  ],
